---
id: org.dxos.plugin.tldraw
name: TldrawPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

A collaborative whiteboard plugin for `DXOS` Composer — powered by tldraw, persisted in ECHO, and available as a first-class workspace object.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`        |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`        |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`        |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`   |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`          |
| `flow`      | `org.dxos.mdl.flow@1.0`        |

## Types

```mdl
type Canvas
  desc: Low-level drawing document backed by a tldraw store.
  fields:
    schema?: string              # external schema reference (default: tldraw.com/2)
    content: Map<string, any>    # tldraw store snapshot — shapes, bindings, assets
```

```mdl
type Sketch
  desc: User-facing whiteboard object that wraps a Canvas.
  fields:
    name?: string
    canvas: Ref<Canvas>          # reference to the tldraw content store
```

```mdl
type SketchGrid
  literals: mesh | dotted
```

```mdl
type Settings
  fields:
    showGrid?: boolean           # display a background grid on the canvas
    gridType?: SketchGrid        # mesh or dotted pattern
```

```mdl
type Scene
  desc: |
    Backend-neutral scene DSL (src/model). A diagram is a set of world objects
    ("face", "hat") composed of elements in object-local units; a compiler maps
    the scene to tldraw records with identity stamped in record meta
    ({ object, element, kind, scale, dialect }) so edits address shapes by id.
  fields:
    objects: WorldObject[]
```

```mdl
type WorldObject
  fields:
    id: string                   # semantic id ("face"); addressing key for edits
    origin?: Point               # canvas px; derived from bbox top-left on read
    scale?: number               # canvas px per local unit (default 1)
    elements: Element[]          # rect | ellipse | circle | diamond | triangle |
                                 # line | curve | arc | text | arrow
```

```mdl
type Command
  desc: Scene edit commands (D2-Oracle-style, addressed by id).
  literals: upsert-object | upsert-elements | remove-elements | remove-object | move-object
```

## Components

```mdl
component SketchArticle
  desc: Full-screen whiteboard surface for a Sketch object. Renders inside article, section, and slide roles.
  props:
    subject: Sketch
    settings: Settings
    attendableId: string
    role: article | section | slide
  state:
    editor?: Editor              # tldraw Editor instance
    hasAttention: boolean
  slots:
    toolbar?: ReactNode          # injected tldraw toolbar actions
  actions:
    createThread()               # opens a comment thread anchored to a selection
  layout: |
    ┌─────────────────────────────────┐
    │ tldraw toolbar (when attended)  │
    ├─────────────────────────────────┤
    │                                 │
    │   infinite canvas (tldraw)      │
    │   shapes / freehand / text      │
    │                                 │
    │   [comment thread anchors]      │
    │                                 │
    └─────────────────────────────────┘
```

```mdl
component SketchSettings
  desc: Settings panel for the Sketch plugin — controls grid visibility and type.
  props:
    settings: Settings
    onSettingsChange?: (updater: (s: Settings) => Settings) => void
```

## Operations

> **Architecture has moved since this section was written.** `plugin-tldraw` no longer owns a
> `Sketch`/`Canvas` type or a `createSketch`/`readSketch`/`editSketch` operation — there is no
> `operations/` directory and no `Sketch` class in `src/` at all. Tldraw is now a **render/create
> variant** contributed to `plugin-illustrator`'s `Drawing` type
> (`src/capabilities/drawing-variant.ts`, `IllustratorCapabilities.VariantProvider`, id
> `tldraw.com/2`) — `TldrawArticle`/`TldrawCard` render a `Drawing.Canvas` whose `schema` is
> `tldraw.com/2`, and the Scene DSL create/read/edit operations documented below actually live in
> `@dxos/plugin-illustrator` (`org.dxos.operation.illustrator.{create,read,edit}`), invoked with
> `variant: 'tldraw.com/2'` to select this plugin's renderer. The type/component sections above
> (`Canvas`, `Sketch`, `Scene`, `WorldObject`, `Command`) and F-7/F-8 below describe the DSL
> correctly in spirit but attribute it to the wrong plugin; QA-1/QA-2 below invoke the real keys.

```mdl
op createSketch
  key: org.dxos.operation.illustrator.create
  desc: |
    Owned by plugin-illustrator, not this plugin (see note above). Creates a Drawing with an
    associated Canvas and adds it to the target space or collection; `variant: 'tldraw.com/2'`
    selects the tldraw renderer instead of another registered DrawingVariant.
  input:
    name?: string
    variant?: string              # canvas typename; here 'tldraw.com/2' — defaults to the first registered variant
  output: { object: Drawing }
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op readSketch
  key: org.dxos.operation.illustrator.read
  desc: |
    Owned by plugin-illustrator (see note above). Returns the derived Scene (world objects with
    object-local coordinates) read from the live canvas records, plus a count of unmanaged
    (hand-drawn) shapes. Origins derive from bounding boxes, so the scene stays coherent after
    users drag shapes. The agent calls this before editing an existing sketch.
  input:
    drawing: Ref<Drawing>
  output: { scene: Scene, unmanaged: number }
  requires: [Database]
```

```mdl
op editSketch
  key: org.dxos.operation.illustrator.edit
  desc: |
    Owned by plugin-illustrator (see note above). Applies scene commands atomically (one
    Obj.update): upsert/move/remove world objects or individual elements by id. Returns the
    resulting scene so the agent can maintain its mental model across turns.
  input:
    drawing: Ref<Drawing>
    commands: Command[]
  output: { scene: Scene, unmanaged: number, upserted: string[], removed: number }
  effects: [echo:write]
  requires: [Database]
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Whiteboard Canvas

  req F-1.1: Each Sketch owns exactly one Canvas; the Canvas holds the full tldraw store snapshot.
  req F-1.2: Canvas content is stored as a plain record in ECHO — no binary blobs.
  req F-1.3: All tldraw shape types (freehand, geometric, text, arrow, image) are supported.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: ECHO Persistence

  req F-2.1:
    when: user makes any edit in the whiteboard
    then: Canvas.content is updated in ECHO within the debounce window

  req F-2.2:
    when: Sketch is opened after a page reload
    then: tldraw store is hydrated from Canvas.content; no drawing is lost

  req F-2.3: Canvas is a separate ECHO object from Sketch so it can be replicated independently.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Real-time Collaboration

  req F-3.1:
    when: two or more peers open the same Sketch
    then: edits by each peer appear on the other's canvas via ECHO replication

  req F-3.2:
    when: a peer is offline and makes edits
    then: changes merge with remote state on reconnection using ECHO CRDT semantics
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Roles and Presentation

  req F-4.1:
    when: role is article
    then: full tldraw toolbar shown when the sketch has attention; hidden otherwise

  req F-4.2:
    when: role is slide
    then: canvas is read-only; zoom capped at 1.5×

  req F-4.3:
    when: role is section
    then: canvas auto-zooms to fit content; no toolbar shown
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Comment Threads

  req F-5.1:
    when: user activates the thread tool in the toolbar
    then: a new comment thread is created anchored to the current selection

  req F-5.2: Thread anchor positions are stored alongside the drawing so they survive reloads.
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Grid Settings

  req F-6.1:
    when: Settings.showGrid is true
    then: a background grid rendered beneath drawing content

  req F-6.2:
    when: Settings.gridType is mesh
    then: a square-mesh grid is shown

  req F-6.3:
    when: Settings.gridType is dotted
    then: a dotted grid is shown
```

```mdl
feat F-7: Create Sketch Operation

  req F-7.1: Plugin contributes op:createSketch to the operation registry.
  req F-7.2:
    when: op:createSketch is invoked
    then: a Sketch + Canvas pair is created and returned; the Sketch is added to the target collection
```

```mdl
feat F-8: Scene DSL and Agent Skill

  req F-8.1: The scene model (src/model) is backend-neutral — no tldraw imports in scene.ts;
    the tldraw compiler (render.ts/read.ts) is one backend, Excalidraw can be added later.
  req F-8.2: Every DSL-generated tldraw record carries meta { object, element, kind, scale, dialect };
    record ids are deterministic (shape:<object>/<element>) so re-rendering an element reuses its id.
  req F-8.3:
    when: op:editSketch upserts elements of an existing object
    then: only records with matching element ids are replaced; sibling elements are untouched
  req F-8.4:
    when: a shape bound by an arrow is removed
    then: its bindings are removed too; no dangling binding records remain
  req F-8.5:
    when: op:readSketch runs after a user drags shapes in the UI
    then: the derived scene reflects the moved geometry (origin = bbox top-left)
  req F-8.6: Plugin contributes the org.dxos.skill.sketch skill (create/read/edit tools +
    DSL instructions: object-local units, semantic ids, read-before-edit workflow).
  req F-8.7: A dialect registry (scene only for now) reserves the extension point for
    mermaid / d2 / sequence / uml-class compilers that emit scene commands.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
test T-1: Create and open sketch
  given: a Composer space is active
  when: op:createSketch runs with name "My Diagram"
  then:
    - a Sketch object is created with name "My Diagram"
    - Sketch.canvas references a new Canvas with empty content
    - Sketch appears in the space object list
```

```mdl
test T-2: Drawing persists across reload
  given: a Sketch is open and the user draws a freehand stroke
  when: the page is reloaded and the Sketch is reopened
  then:
    - the stroke is visible on the canvas
    - Canvas.content is non-empty
```

```mdl
test T-3: Collaborative edit
  given: two peers have the same Sketch open
  when: peer A draws a rectangle
  then:
    - peer B sees the rectangle appear within the ECHO sync window
    - no data loss if both peers edit simultaneously
```

```mdl
test T-4: Read-only slide role
  given: a Sketch is rendered in role slide
  then:
    - tldraw toolbar is not shown
    - all drawing tools are disabled
    - zoom is capped at 1.5×
```

```mdl
test T-5: Grid toggle
  given: SketchSettings panel is open
  when: user enables the grid and selects "dotted"
  then:
    - Settings.showGrid === true
    - Settings.gridType === dotted
    - dotted grid appears on the canvas immediately
```

```mdl
test T-6: Attention-aware toolbar
  given: a Sketch is open in article role alongside other articles
  when: user clicks on the sketch to give it attention
  then: tldraw toolbar becomes visible
  when: user clicks away, removing attention
  then: tldraw toolbar is hidden
```

```mdl
test T-7: Scene DSL round-trip
  given: an empty Sketch
  when: editSketch upserts a "face" object (head/eyes/smile), then upserts a "hat" object and
    replaces only the "smile" element, then removes the "hat"
  then:
    - readSketch returns the face with derived origin and all element ids
    - the untouched face elements are byte-identical across the hat edit
    - removing the hat removes exactly its records and no bindings dangle
  # Covered by src/operations/operations.test.ts and src/model/scene.test.ts.
```

```mdl
test T-8: Conversational drawing (live AI)
  given: the stories-assistant Sketch storybook (config.remote) with the sketch skill bound
  when: the user prompts "Draw a smiley face", then "Add a hat"
  then:
    - the agent creates a "face" world object via editSketch
    - the follow-up adds a "hat" object WITHOUT redrawing the face (mental-model test)
  # Manual: stories/stories-assistant/Sketch → DrawAndUpdateTest / Reflection (tags: ['!test']).
  # Verified live 2026-07-23 (remote EDGE, claude-opus-4-8): face drawn, hat composed on top,
  # face records untouched.
```

---

## QA

Executable flows. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by flow and step number.
Tldraw is enabled by default in every environment (`plugin-defs.tsx` `getDefaults`).

```mdl
flow QA-1: Create a tldraw sketch and draw on it
  desc: The core whiteboard round-trip — create a Drawing bound to the tldraw variant, draw, reload.
  actors: both
  covers: [F-1.1, F-1.2, F-2.1, F-2.2, T-1, T-2]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - collection: a collection in that space, to create into
    - no Drawing named "QA Sketch" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this flow did not create
  test:
    - name: Create the sketch
      do: In the navtree, click + on a collection and choose Sketch (tldraw). Name it "QA Sketch".
      invoke: [op:createSketch] { name: "QA Sketch", variant: "tldraw.com/2" }
      capture: created
      expect: a Drawing named "QA Sketch" opens in TldrawArticle with an empty canvas
      assert: return !!$created.object
    - name: Place it in the collection
      do: (no separate gesture — the navtree create action places it)
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.addObject { object: $created.object, target: $given.collection }
      expect: "QA Sketch" appears as a row under the collection
    - name: Draw a shape
      do: With the sketch open and focused (attention), select the rectangle tool and draw a rectangle on the canvas.
      expect: the rectangle appears on the canvas
      note: |
        NO `invoke` — freehand drawing is a pointer gesture inside the tldraw canvas, with no
        operation behind it; the DSL ops (`op:editSketch`) address semantic world objects, not
        raw hand-drawn shapes. This step is human-only.
  after:
    - name: Delete the sketch
      do: Right-click "QA Sketch" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$created.object], target: $given.collection }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and its plank closes if it was open
```

```mdl
flow QA-2: Scene DSL round-trip — draw a face, then add a hat without redrawing it
  desc: |
    The agent-facing DSL path (F-8 / T-7): create, read, and edit a scene addressed by semantic
    object ids, verifying an edit to one world object leaves siblings untouched.
  actors: agent
  covers: [F-7.1, F-7.2, F-8.2, F-8.3, T-7]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - collection: a collection in that space, to create into
    - no Drawing named "QA Face" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this flow did not create
  test:
    - name: Create the sketch
      do: (agent-only step — DSL editing has no human equivalent gesture; a human would draw freehand instead)
      invoke: [op:createSketch] { name: "QA Face", variant: "tldraw.com/2" }
      capture: created
      expect: an empty Drawing named "QA Face" is created
      assert: return !!$created.object
    - name: Place it in the collection
      do: (no separate gesture)
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.addObject { object: $created.object, target: $given.collection }
      expect: "QA Face" appears as a row under the collection
    - name: Draw a face
      do: (no human gesture — this is the DSL path)
      invoke: |
        org.dxos.operation.illustrator.edit {
          drawing: $created.object,
          commands: [{ kind: "upsert-object", id: "face", elements: [
            { id: "head", type: "circle" },
            { id: "smile", type: "arc" }
          ] }]
        }
      capture: withFace
      expect: the canvas renders a circle ("head") and an arc ("smile"); reading the scene returns
        a "face" object with both element ids
      assert: return $result.upserted.includes('face')
    - name: Add a hat without touching the face
      do: (no human gesture — this is the DSL path)
      invoke: |
        org.dxos.operation.illustrator.edit {
          drawing: $created.object,
          commands: [{ kind: "upsert-object", id: "hat", elements: [{ id: "brim", type: "triangle" }] }]
        }
      expect: the canvas now also renders the hat; the face's "head" and "smile" records are
        byte-identical to the previous step's — the edit touched only the "hat" object
      assert: return $result.upserted.includes('hat') && !$result.upserted.includes('face')
      note: |
        This is the mental-model regression T-8 describes for live AI conversation — asserting on
        `upserted` (which object ids the edit actually touched) is the falsifiable form of "the
        face was not redrawn," per Rule 5.
  after:
    - name: Delete the sketch
      do: Right-click "QA Face" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$created.object], target: $given.collection }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and its plank closes if it was open
```

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

```mdl
ext type
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0
  desc: A named data structure with typed fields and optional literals.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    fields?: FieldMap
    literals?: UnionList
    extends?: TypeRef[]
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self
```

```mdl
ext test
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

```mdl
ext component
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0
  desc: A UI component with props, internal state, slots, actions, and events.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    props?: FieldMap
    state?: FieldMap
    slots?: FieldMap
    actions?: ActionMap
    emits?: EventMap
    layout?: CodeBlock
```

```mdl
ext op
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.op@1.0
  desc: |
    A named operation with typed inputs, outputs, and declared errors.
    Pure ops have no effects or requires. Effectful ops declare both.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    input?: FieldMap
    output?: TypeExpr
    errors?: ErrorMap
    effects?: EffectList
    requires?: ServiceList
    note?: Prose
```
